@Chris

He says "Yo, Adrian" in the Rocky movies. 

Incredibly funny to put it in the Tricky Clues section and then not explain it.

@Chris

Rocky was from Philadelphia. “Yo” is common slang there. The beginning of one of that character’s more famous lines was “Yo, Adrian…”

Back in the ‘70s, I was an undergrad at Penn State, which is roughly in the center of the state. It had plenty of kids from Philadelphia and Pittsburgh. We used to say we were stuck between the “yinz” and the “yos.”  Yinz was Pittsburgh slang pronunciation for “you’uns.”

